  "starterCode": "import torch\n\ndef pytorch_softmax_from_scratch(logits: list) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Softmax from Scratch** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport torch, numpy as np\n\ndef pytorch_softmax_from_scratch(logits: list) -> list:\n    z = torch.tensor(logits, dtype=torch.float32)\n    ex = torch.exp(z - torch.max(z, dim=-1, keepdim=True).values)\n    return np.round((ex / torch.sum(ex, dim=-1, keepdim=True)).numpy(), 6).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
